hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15634","Al-Haytham ibn Kharijah said: Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And I heard it from al-Haytham. Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Walid, from Abu Mansur, the freed slave of the Ansar, from Amr ibn al-Jamuh, that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The servant does not attain the right of pure faith until he loves for Allah Almighty and hates for Allah. When he loves for Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and hates for Allah, Blessed and Exalted, he has deserved loyalty from Allah. Indeed my allies among My servants and My beloved among My creation are those who are remembered by My remembrance and I am remembered by their remembrance."
